\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of the core event-timing tests to the Rousseau et al. KS detection-window choice. Values are p-values for the complete 0.4--4 kyr and 0.6--4 kyr transition catalogues. Asterisks indicate \(p < 0.05\). The ``Consistent'' column indicates that the same significance decision (\(p<0.05\) or \(p\geq 0.05\)) is reached for both KS window choices.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ks_window_core_sensitivity}{{S1}{5}{}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces  Additional-forcing sensitivity tests relative to the extended baseline model. The extended baseline contains same-type event history, Cheng composite sampling resolution, LR04, \(\ce {CO2}\), and precession phase. For ``Add'' tests, the reduced model is the extended baseline and the full model adds the listed forcing or forcing set. For ``unique'' tests, the reduced model is the model with all extra forcings except the listed forcing and the full model contains all extra forcings. \(\Delta \)AICc is full minus reduced; negative values favor the added term. None of the likelihood-ratio tests is significant at \(p<0.05\). }}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:additional_forcing_sensitivity}{{S2}{6}{}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S3}{\ignorespaces  Reduced-model parametric bootstrap likelihood-ratio diagnostics for the two central adjusted predictive-model comparisons. The bootstrap regenerated event catalogues under the fitted reduced model, recomputed same-type event history, and refitted the reduced and full models for each replicate. This preserves the serial dependence induced by overlapping 5 kyr history windows. The empirical \(p\) value is \((1+\#\{\mathrm  {LR}^{(b)}\geq \mathrm  {LR}_{\mathrm  {obs}}\})/(1+B)\), with \(B=2000\). }}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bootstrap_lrt_diagnostics}{{S3}{6}{}{table.3}{}}
