\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S8}{\ignorespaces  Conditional lagged predictive information from precession phase for (a) strong and (b) weak monsoon starts. Curves show the additional predictive-information gain, in bits per event, from adding lagged precession phase after the event-process baseline and LR04~\citep  {lisiecki2005pliocene}+\(\ce {CO2}\)~\citep  {bereiter2015revision} controls. Blue curves condition on LR04 and \(\ce {CO2}\) sampled at the same lag as precession phase; orange curves condition on LR04 and \(\ce {CO2}\) fixed at their best single-driver lags. Open circles mark lag points that remain significant after Benjamini--Hochberg false-discovery-rate correction (\(q\leq 0.05\)). }}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conditional_lagged_precession}{{S8}{12}{}{figure.8}{}}
